{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>For the needy will not cease.</b> Above, where it writes 'only there will be no needy among you' — this is on condition: there will be no needy among you — only if you indeed obey. Here, where it says <b>for the needy will not cease</b>, this is the language of 'perhaps' — perhaps you will not prepare your deeds fully enough. In this chapter there are four instances of כי serving four meanings: 'כי יהיה בך אביון' — the sense of 'if'; 'כי פתוח תפתח' — the sense of 'rather' (אלא); 'כי בגלל הדבר הזה' — the sense of 'because' (דהא). <b>For the needy will not cease</b> — this is the language of 'perhaps,' perhaps you will not make your deeds worthy in every respect." "<b>To your brother.</b> The close relative takes precedence." "<b>To your poor.</b> From your family." "<b>And to your pauper in your land.</b> Those in your city take precedence."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:52:57.657551446Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}